  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe coldest air of the season will continue into the weekend. \nHigher elevations of the northern West Virginia mountains \nalready have a coating of snow. A couple of short waves will \nmove across the area this afternoon and evening, and early \nSaturday, enhancing precipitation. Friday night into Saturday, a\nnorthwesterly wind flow and cold air advection will create \nupslope snow conditions, even though 850 mb temperatures are not\nquite in the ideal range. The combination of these events will \nallow for another inch or two of snow in the higher elevations \nof the mountains. Boundary layer temperatures will remain \nmarginal for snow in the lowlands. If snow does occur in those \nlocations, ground temperatures should be too warm for any \naccumulations.",
